WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.701
Joe: [British accent] From
calorie count to portion sizes,

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:03.570
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:04.704
between Dunkin' Donuts –

00:00:04.704 --> 00:00:06.272
haha, it's me!

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:07.307
OK, I'll do it for real.

00:00:09.009 --> 00:00:10.677
From calorie count to portion sizes,

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:12.545
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:15.348
between Dunkin' Donuts
in the UK and the US.

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:16.950
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:21.654 --> 00:00:22.789
At Dunkin' Donuts in the US,

00:00:22.789 --> 00:00:24.824
you can get your doughnuts
in three different...

00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:25.925
sizes, I guess?

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:27.761
One doughnut,

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:31.531
half a dozen doughnuts, nice,

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:34.067
and, of course, everyone's favorite,

00:00:34.067 --> 00:00:35.935
dozen doughnuts.

00:00:36.403 --> 00:00:37.871
Harry: In the UK, our doughnuts also come

00:00:37.871 --> 00:00:39.205
in three quantities,

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:41.608
and, shockingly, it's the
same as in the States.

00:00:42.475 --> 00:00:43.343
You can get one doughnut,

00:00:43.343 --> 00:00:45.578
a half dozen doughnuts,

00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:48.782
or you can be the life of the party

00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:50.984
with the full dozen.

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:53.186
Joe: And it's "Food Wars," so you know

00:00:53.186 --> 00:00:54.954
we're weighing a doughnut.

00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:56.423
Harry: Now let's see how
much a glazed doughnut

00:00:56.423 --> 00:00:57.490
weighs in the UK.

00:01:01.294 --> 00:01:02.228
Our glazed doughnut came to

00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:03.696
pretty much exactly 50 grams,

00:01:03.696 --> 00:01:05.665
so it looks like the States
are getting a better deal.

00:01:06.132 --> 00:01:07.367
Joe: At a US Dunkin' Donuts,

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:08.568
you can get your Munchkins

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:11.371
in four different units of Munchkin.

00:01:13.073 --> 00:01:14.340
Five Munchkins.

00:01:17.177 --> 00:01:19.145
10 Munchkins.

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:20.713
Not enough?

00:01:20.713 --> 00:01:23.283
Kick it up to 25 Munchkins.

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:23.983
See that?

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:25.318
And if that isn't enough,

00:01:25.318 --> 00:01:29.456
you can go all the way to 50 Munchkins.

00:01:29.456 --> 00:01:30.490
50 of these things!

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:31.925
Wow, look at the size of this!

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:33.093
It's a lot of Munchkins.

00:01:33.293 --> 00:01:36.029
Harry: In the UK, we also
have four units of Munchkin,

00:01:36.029 --> 00:01:38.364
starting with four.

00:01:39.466 --> 00:01:42.102
From there, we move upwards to...

00:01:44.137 --> 00:01:45.405
12 Munchkins.

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:47.474
The next size up from 12

00:01:47.474 --> 00:01:48.608
is in a box,

00:01:48.608 --> 00:01:50.009
and the box contains...

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:52.745
24 Munchkins.

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:54.013
And, finally,

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:56.950
our biggest size of Munchkins in the UK

00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:57.984
is 50.

00:02:01.221 --> 00:02:02.489
Now, it might not make too much sense

00:02:02.489 --> 00:02:04.958
to compare just one Munchkin
in the UK and the US,

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:05.825
because I'm sure they're all

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:07.427
slightly different shapes and sizes.

00:02:07.427 --> 00:02:08.595
However, what we could do is

00:02:08.595 --> 00:02:11.965
measure 24 Munchkins here
and 24 Munchkins there

00:02:11.965 --> 00:02:13.933
and hope that it provides
a kind of overview

00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:15.068
of the average weight.

00:02:15.068 --> 00:02:16.002
That sound about right?

00:02:16.336 --> 00:02:17.570
Joe: Sounds like science to me.

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:18.404
Let's do it.

00:02:18.404 --> 00:02:19.405
All right.

00:02:19.405 --> 00:02:21.608
This is 25, so I'm going to take one out.

00:02:24.611 --> 00:02:26.079
Harry: Can I do it without spilling?

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:28.448
Oh, God.

00:02:28.448 --> 00:02:29.482
Joe: Whoop.

00:02:29.482 --> 00:02:30.817
Harry: [laughing] Oh, God.

00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:36.756
Looking like a croquembouche.

00:02:42.295 --> 00:02:44.063
What, how is that so good?

00:02:44.063 --> 00:02:45.999
OK. Munchkin challenge No. 1:

00:02:45.999 --> 00:02:47.567
How many Munchkins can I fit in my mouth

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:49.736
at one time without dying?

00:02:50.837 --> 00:02:53.339
[jazzy music]

00:02:54.274 --> 00:02:55.909
Cameraman: I'm not ready.

00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:05.585
Joe: Can you hurry this up, man?

00:03:05.585 --> 00:03:06.419
We got other stuff to --

00:03:06.419 --> 00:03:07.587
ahhh!

00:03:08.588 --> 00:03:10.690
[laughs]

00:03:14.961 --> 00:03:17.430
If you guessed seven,
you were roughly right.

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:18.698
Although I felt like I sort of cheated,

00:03:18.698 --> 00:03:20.700
because I almost died.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:21.834
Joe: In the US Dunkin' Donuts,

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:24.137
our hot coffees come in four sizes.

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:26.573
Small.
Harry: In the UK,

00:03:26.573 --> 00:03:28.174
our hot coffees come in two sizes,

00:03:28.174 --> 00:03:29.409
regular and large.

00:03:32.145 --> 00:03:34.147
Joe: Large

00:03:34.147 --> 00:03:35.548
and

00:03:35.548 --> 00:03:37.250
extra large.

00:03:38.451 --> 00:03:39.786
The Dunkin' Donuts US website

00:03:39.786 --> 00:03:42.455
says that their large
hot coffee is 20 ounces.

00:03:42.455 --> 00:03:43.723
Got a measuring cup here,

00:03:43.723 --> 00:03:45.358
let's find out if that is true.

00:03:45.491 --> 00:03:47.527
Now, full disclosure,

00:03:47.527 --> 00:03:49.362
on the car ride over here,

00:03:49.362 --> 00:03:51.264
had a little bit of a spillage.

00:03:51.264 --> 00:03:53.566
So I'm gonna give this one,

00:03:53.566 --> 00:03:55.268
we'll say, a 2-ounce leeway.

00:03:55.268 --> 00:03:57.937
Should be 20 ounces, might be 18.

00:03:57.937 --> 00:03:59.372
Yo!

00:04:01.074 --> 00:04:02.442
OK, that's 16.

00:04:02.709 --> 00:04:03.977
4 more ounces.

00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:06.980
[blows a raspberry]

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:09.716
Give me a break!

00:04:09.716 --> 00:04:11.284
That's maybe an ounce.

00:04:11.284 --> 00:04:14.320
16 plus one, I think, is still 17.

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:16.256
There is no way

00:04:16.256 --> 00:04:17.590
there is

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:19.359
this much of coffee

00:04:19.359 --> 00:04:20.660
on my car seat.

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:22.562
Let's generously add 2 –

00:04:22.562 --> 00:04:24.430
16, 17, 18, 19 –

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:25.398
I don't want to be that generous.

00:04:25.498 --> 00:04:26.532
Wait a second.

00:04:26.532 --> 00:04:27.367
I got an idea.

00:04:27.367 --> 00:04:30.203
20 ounces, so that means
I need 4 in here, correct?

00:04:32.905 --> 00:04:34.874
OK. That's 20 ounces.

00:04:37.176 --> 00:04:38.678
I'm gonna settle this right now.

00:04:44.417 --> 00:04:48.321
OK. There's 16 in a cup, plus 4.

00:04:48.321 --> 00:04:49.522
You know what's about to happen.

00:04:49.522 --> 00:04:50.356
You ready?

00:04:50.356 --> 00:04:53.426
[suspenseful music]

00:05:06.973 --> 00:05:07.807
Come on, now.

00:05:08.007 --> 00:05:09.275
Harry: Now, that all seems very dramatic,

00:05:09.275 --> 00:05:11.577
so I'm also gonna
measure our large coffee.

00:05:13.079 --> 00:05:13.946
Not a black coffee.

00:05:13.946 --> 00:05:14.847
Did I get that with milk?

00:05:14.847 --> 00:05:15.648
I'm so stupid.

00:05:15.782 --> 00:05:17.784
I just remembered I put milk in the large.

00:05:17.784 --> 00:05:19.118
So, we're going to measure anyway

00:05:19.118 --> 00:05:20.086
and see what happens.

00:05:23.856 --> 00:05:27.193
Looks pretty much exactly 16 ounces.

00:05:27.393 --> 00:05:28.394
Iced coffees in the UK

00:05:28.394 --> 00:05:31.030
also come in two sizes, regular and large.

00:05:31.264 --> 00:05:32.632
Joe: At a Dunkin' Donuts in the US,

00:05:32.632 --> 00:05:34.801
we have three iced-coffee sizes,

00:05:35.935 --> 00:05:37.370
small,

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:38.671
mediums,

00:05:38.671 --> 00:05:40.973
and the large.

00:05:41.341 --> 00:05:42.975
Harry: [laughing] No one needs, like,

00:05:42.975 --> 00:05:44.277
32 ounces of coffee.

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:45.545
That's just too much.

00:05:45.878 --> 00:05:47.180
Joe: 32 ounces.

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:48.514
Do I have enough for 32 ounces?

00:05:48.514 --> 00:05:51.351
This is 16, and this is...

00:05:51.351 --> 00:05:52.585
8. No, I don't.

00:05:52.819 --> 00:05:54.587
Harry: We're also gonna
measure our large iced coffee

00:05:54.587 --> 00:05:55.521
to see what it comes to.

00:06:01.994 --> 00:06:04.897
So, a large iced coffee in
the UK came to 18 ounces.

00:06:05.131 --> 00:06:09.102
Joe: Since I don't have
another 16-ounce cup,

00:06:09.102 --> 00:06:10.803
I will use this one.

00:06:15.475 --> 00:06:17.844
Right on the 16.

00:06:17.844 --> 00:06:20.413
OK. That's one 16 ounce.

00:06:21.781 --> 00:06:22.682
Oh, jeez.

00:06:22.682 --> 00:06:24.751
This is exactly 16 ounces here.

00:06:24.751 --> 00:06:26.686
Was this the large?

00:06:26.686 --> 00:06:28.821
Conner: I think that was the large, yeah.

00:06:28.821 --> 00:06:31.891
Joe: This should be 16 more fluid ounces.

00:06:35.661 --> 00:06:36.829
Shameful.

00:06:36.829 --> 00:06:39.499
Absolutely shameful.

00:06:39.499 --> 00:06:41.167
There definitely was not

00:06:41.167 --> 00:06:42.869
this much space left in the cup.

00:06:42.869 --> 00:06:44.937
27 1/2 fluid ounces

00:06:44.937 --> 00:06:48.474
in your 32-ounce large iced coffee.

00:06:48.474 --> 00:06:50.410
It's still almost to the, I mean –

00:06:50.410 --> 00:06:51.611
our PA just pointed out

00:06:51.611 --> 00:06:53.379
that maybe the density is different,

00:06:53.379 --> 00:06:55.581
right when you put exactly
the most frozen ice?

00:06:55.581 --> 00:06:56.649
Maybe.

00:06:56.649 --> 00:06:59.585
Well, let's ask someone who's a scientist.

00:06:59.585 --> 00:07:00.019
[laughs]

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:02.255
Harry: Not a scientist, but
that won't change anything,

00:07:02.255 --> 00:07:04.557
and you guys are still kind
of getting a bit shortchanged.

00:07:04.557 --> 00:07:05.925
It's just 'cause the density

00:07:05.925 --> 00:07:08.194
of the solid or the liquid might change.

00:07:08.194 --> 00:07:09.462
The actual amount of liquid in there

00:07:09.462 --> 00:07:10.396
is still going to be the same,

00:07:10.396 --> 00:07:12.165
so it should all balance
itself out eventually.

00:07:12.498 --> 00:07:13.633
Joe: At the US Dunkin' Donuts,

00:07:13.633 --> 00:07:15.902
the largest single food item you can get

00:07:15.902 --> 00:07:17.703
is this, two dozen doughnuts,

00:07:17.703 --> 00:07:20.640
and the largest drink you can get is

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:21.841
a Box O' Joe.

00:07:21.841 --> 00:07:22.675
Look at this.

00:07:22.675 --> 00:07:24.944
Think that's about 100
fluid ounces of coffee.

00:07:25.144 --> 00:07:26.245
I've always wanted to do this.

00:07:26.245 --> 00:07:27.480
It's, like, really hot in here.

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:28.314
OK.

00:07:30.883 --> 00:07:32.418
Ahh!

00:07:32.418 --> 00:07:35.121
Just set this down on my seat and be like,

00:07:35.121 --> 00:07:36.856
"This is my coffee.

00:07:36.856 --> 00:07:37.690
All right?"

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:39.592
Then write my name right
on it, right there.

00:07:39.592 --> 00:07:41.260
"Joe, do not touch."

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:42.094
Conner: It's already on it.

00:07:42.094 --> 00:07:43.196
Joe: What? Is it?

00:07:43.196 --> 00:07:44.931
Oh, yeah. [laughs]

00:07:44.931 --> 00:07:46.365
Mine, baby!

00:07:46.365 --> 00:07:47.867
Mine!

00:07:48.201 --> 00:07:50.269
Oh, man, I've already
drank way too much coffee.

00:07:50.269 --> 00:07:51.904
[laughs]

00:07:52.939 --> 00:07:54.841
Harry: Now, the biggest
thing on the menu in the UK

00:07:54.841 --> 00:07:56.142
is the Dunkin' Feast.

00:07:56.142 --> 00:07:58.611
This is two dozen doughnuts, 50 Munchkins,

00:07:58.611 --> 00:08:00.580
and two Boxes O' Joe,

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:02.448
all for a price of 80 pounds.

00:08:02.715 --> 00:08:03.983
Now, unfortunately, when we went in today,

00:08:03.983 --> 00:08:06.052
they didn't have any
Boxes O' Joe available.

00:08:06.052 --> 00:08:08.054
However, one of them is supposed to be

00:08:08.054 --> 00:08:09.522
100 fluid ounces of coffee,

00:08:09.522 --> 00:08:11.357
which is far too much coffee.

00:08:11.357 --> 00:08:12.024
Joe: [laughs]

00:08:14.126 --> 00:08:17.263
This here is a US glazed
Dunkin' Donut doughnut.

00:08:17.263 --> 00:08:21.300
It is roughly 360 calories,
has 22 grams of fat,

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:22.502
10 of those are saturated,

00:08:22.502 --> 00:08:25.538
420 milligrams of sodium, 39 carbs,

00:08:25.538 --> 00:08:27.306
and 18 grams of sugar.

00:08:27.773 --> 00:08:31.277
Harry: And in the UK, the same
doughnut has 230 calories,

00:08:31.277 --> 00:08:34.447
13 grams of fat, 230 milligrams of sodium,

00:08:34.447 --> 00:08:37.149
25 grams of carbs, and 10 grams of sugar.

00:08:37.416 --> 00:08:39.919
Joe: So, by my calculations,
the US glazed doughnut

00:08:39.919 --> 00:08:42.688
is 56.5% higher in calories,

00:08:42.688 --> 00:08:44.924
69.2% higher in fat,

00:08:44.924 --> 00:08:46.826
and 80% higher in sugar.

00:08:46.859 --> 00:08:48.628
I gotta burp. [burps]

00:08:48.628 --> 00:08:49.328
Sorry.

00:08:49.462 --> 00:08:50.830
Let's talk about another doughnut,

00:08:50.830 --> 00:08:52.832
the Boston Kreme doughnut.

00:08:52.832 --> 00:08:54.267
I don't know why it's shaped like a heart.

00:08:54.267 --> 00:08:55.601
I'm assuming 'cause it's Valentine's.

00:08:55.601 --> 00:08:57.136
We're shooting this in February.

00:08:57.169 --> 00:08:58.638
Normally, it's a circle.

00:08:58.804 --> 00:09:01.107
Anyway, this doughnut has

00:09:01.107 --> 00:09:03.209
270 calories,

00:09:03.209 --> 00:09:05.778
11 grams of fat, 18 grams of sugar.

00:09:06.045 --> 00:09:07.547
Harry: The UK version of the Boston Kreme

00:09:07.547 --> 00:09:09.115
contains 280 calories,

00:09:09.115 --> 00:09:11.784
15 grams of fat, 17 grams of sugar.

00:09:11.817 --> 00:09:14.086
So that has more calories and fat.

00:09:14.353 --> 00:09:16.289
Joe: A large iced coffee
with cream and sugar,

00:09:16.289 --> 00:09:18.958
in the US, has roughly 260 cu –

00:09:18.958 --> 00:09:20.593
[blows a raspberry]

00:09:21.093 --> 00:09:22.562
Hang on.
Conner: Yeah.

00:09:23.796 --> 00:09:26.132
Joe: [claps] Back to life, baby!

00:09:26.132 --> 00:09:28.901
A large iced coffee at a
Dunkin' Donuts in the US

00:09:28.901 --> 00:09:30.803
has 260 calories,

00:09:30.803 --> 00:09:32.104
18 grams of fat,

00:09:32.104 --> 00:09:34.440
and 37 grams of carbs.

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:36.208
That seems like a lot, doesn't it?

00:09:36.442 --> 00:09:38.311
Harry: In the UK, a large Dunkin' coffee

00:09:38.311 --> 00:09:40.980
with cream and sugar
comes to 190 calories,

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:45.051
with 9.1 grams of fat
and 30.4 grams of carbs.

00:09:45.351 --> 00:09:47.386
Joe: If we break it down by fluid ounce,

00:09:47.386 --> 00:09:48.821
it turns out the US is higher

00:09:48.821 --> 00:09:51.257
in every metric except carbs.

00:09:51.257 --> 00:09:52.992
Just look at all that data.

00:09:53.292 --> 00:09:55.061
Thinking about adding a
flavor pump to your coffee?

00:09:55.428 --> 00:09:56.629
In the US and the UK,

00:09:56.629 --> 00:09:58.998
you can get vanilla,
caramel, hazelnut flavors.

00:09:58.998 --> 00:10:00.933
On average in the US, though,

00:10:00.933 --> 00:10:01.834
when you add those pumps,

00:10:01.834 --> 00:10:04.470
you are adding 165 calories,

00:10:04.470 --> 00:10:06.005
38 grams of carbs,

00:10:06.005 --> 00:10:08.874
and 37 more grams of sugar.

00:10:09.308 --> 00:10:10.710
All of our information from the UK

00:10:10.710 --> 00:10:13.079
for this episode was taken from

00:10:13.079 --> 00:10:14.680
not Dunkin' Donuts UK,

00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:17.617
but other nutrition sites

00:10:17.617 --> 00:10:19.485
and food bloggers and whatever.

00:10:19.752 --> 00:10:20.820
Assuming that the iced coffee

00:10:20.820 --> 00:10:22.755
in the US and [UK] Dunkin'
Donuts are the same,

00:10:22.755 --> 00:10:24.223
not sure if it is, they didn't tell us,

00:10:24.223 --> 00:10:25.691
thanks a lot, Dunkin' Donuts UK,

00:10:25.691 --> 00:10:26.993
but assuming it is the same,

00:10:26.993 --> 00:10:29.495
to get this large iced
coffee with cream and sugar

00:10:29.495 --> 00:10:31.397
and these two doughnuts
we talked about earlier,

00:10:31.397 --> 00:10:34.433
total, it is 890 calories,

00:10:34.433 --> 00:10:37.937
which is 35.6% of your daily intake.

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:38.738
Harry: And in the UK,

00:10:38.738 --> 00:10:40.539
a large iced coffee with cream and sugar,

00:10:40.539 --> 00:10:42.274
a glazed doughnut, and
a Boston Kreme doughnut

00:10:42.274 --> 00:10:43.843
comes to 700 calories,

00:10:43.843 --> 00:10:46.445
or 28% of your daily allowance.

00:10:46.679 --> 00:10:47.446
Joe: What about Munchkins?

00:10:47.446 --> 00:10:50.816
In the US, one glazed
Munchkin is 60 calories,

00:10:50.816 --> 00:10:53.986
3 grams of fat, 60 milligrams of sodium,

00:10:53.986 --> 00:10:56.589
7 grams of carbs, and 3 grams of sugar.

00:10:59.291 --> 00:11:00.660
Harry: Now, unfortunately,
Dunkin' in the UK

00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:03.095
does not release any of its
ingredients information.

00:11:03.095 --> 00:11:04.964
We did reach out to see if
they'd make an exception,

00:11:04.964 --> 00:11:06.465
but unfortunately, at the
time we're shooting this,

00:11:06.465 --> 00:11:07.299
they had not.

00:11:07.400 --> 00:11:09.168
Joe: US Dunkin' Donuts' website does have

00:11:09.168 --> 00:11:11.337
a majority of its
nutritional info on the site.

00:11:11.337 --> 00:11:12.772
Let me read you some hits right now.

00:11:12.772 --> 00:11:14.840
OK, first, the coffee. Hot or cold,

00:11:14.840 --> 00:11:17.743
it's 100% brewed arabica coffee.

00:11:17.743 --> 00:11:18.577
Fantastic.

00:11:18.577 --> 00:11:19.845
Now, if you want to add

00:11:19.845 --> 00:11:20.980
cream and sugar to your coffee

00:11:20.980 --> 00:11:22.682
like a 16-year-old influencer,

00:11:22.682 --> 00:11:24.550
now you've added milk, cream,

00:11:24.550 --> 00:11:26.819
disodium phosphate as a stabilizer,

00:11:26.819 --> 00:11:28.721
sodium citrate as a stabilizer,

00:11:28.721 --> 00:11:29.789
and sugar.

00:11:30.222 --> 00:11:31.590
Of the many flavor shots

00:11:31.590 --> 00:11:32.825
you can add to the coffee in the US,

00:11:32.825 --> 00:11:33.793
I picked the caramel one,

00:11:33.793 --> 00:11:34.960
'cause it's also available in the UK,

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:36.495
assuming that it is the same

00:11:36.495 --> 00:11:37.763
in the US and the UK.

00:11:37.763 --> 00:11:40.132
In the US, the caramel
shots are made up of

00:11:40.132 --> 00:11:42.368
sweetened condensed nonfat milk,

00:11:42.368 --> 00:11:44.270
which is nonfat milk and sugar,

00:11:44.270 --> 00:11:45.771
high-fructose corn syrup,

00:11:45.771 --> 00:11:48.441
and sugar, water, and brown sugar,

00:11:48.441 --> 00:11:50.943
so three different
various sugar substances.

00:11:50.943 --> 00:11:51.777
Fantastic.

00:11:51.777 --> 00:11:52.611
Caramel color,

00:11:52.611 --> 00:11:54.413
potassium sorbate as a preservative,

00:11:54.413 --> 00:11:56.649
natural flavors, and salt.

00:11:57.283 --> 00:11:59.552
A glazed doughnut at a US Dunkin' Donuts

00:11:59.552 --> 00:12:01.654
is made up of enriched wheat flour,

00:12:01.654 --> 00:12:04.023
which is flour, malted barley –

00:12:04.023 --> 00:12:05.391
[laughs]

00:12:05.658 --> 00:12:06.859
Holy s---. OK.

00:12:07.193 --> 00:12:10.429
Niacin, reduced iron,
thiamine mononitrate,

00:12:10.429 --> 00:12:12.164
riboflavin, folic acid,

00:12:12.164 --> 00:12:13.432
all right,

00:12:13.432 --> 00:12:15.067
water, palm oil,

00:12:15.067 --> 00:12:16.769
yeast doughnut concentrate,

00:12:16.769 --> 00:12:19.305
brackets, which is soy flour, salt,

00:12:19.305 --> 00:12:20.906
leavening,

00:12:20.906 --> 00:12:24.410
sodium acid pyrophosphate,

00:12:24.410 --> 00:12:25.311
baking soda,

00:12:25.311 --> 00:12:26.145
[sighs]

00:12:26.145 --> 00:12:29.215
wheat starch, whey (a milk derivative),

00:12:29.215 --> 00:12:31.083
nonfat dry milk,

00:12:31.083 --> 00:12:32.351
gum blend,

00:12:32.351 --> 00:12:36.155
which is cellulous gum,
guar gum, acacia gum,

00:12:36.155 --> 00:12:39.358
carrageenan, and xanthan gum.

00:12:39.358 --> 00:12:40.326
A lot of gum.

00:12:40.326 --> 00:12:41.560
Can you scroll up, please?

00:12:41.560 --> 00:12:43.062
[clears throat]

00:12:43.062 --> 00:12:47.133
Sodium caseinate, which
is a milk derivative,

00:12:47.199 --> 00:12:49.034
sodium stearloyl lassithate,

00:12:49.435 --> 00:12:50.269
lass-,

00:12:50.269 --> 00:12:51.403
lactylate,

00:12:51.403 --> 00:12:53.539
and it contains 2% or less of

00:12:53.539 --> 00:12:55.908
soybean oil, soy lecithin,

00:12:55.908 --> 00:12:57.843
whole egg, natural flavors,

00:12:57.843 --> 00:13:00.546
turmeric extract for color, enzymes,

00:13:00.546 --> 00:13:03.382
annatto extract for
color, yeast, dextrose,

00:13:03.382 --> 00:13:06.418
soybean oil, and mono and diglycerides.

00:13:06.418 --> 00:13:07.953
OK, that's the dough.

00:13:07.953 --> 00:13:09.054
Now for the glaze!

00:13:09.054 --> 00:13:10.322
We ain't even done yet.

00:13:10.322 --> 00:13:11.323
Scroll up, please.

00:13:11.323 --> 00:13:13.058
The glaze of a glazed doughnut has

00:13:13.058 --> 00:13:14.860
sugar, water, maltodextrin,

00:13:14.860 --> 00:13:17.997
and contains 2% or less of cornstarch,

00:13:17.997 --> 00:13:21.667
mono and diglycerides, citric acid, agar,

00:13:21.667 --> 00:13:24.837
cellulose gum, potassium
sorbate as a preservative,

00:13:24.837 --> 00:13:27.072
and, of course, artificial flavors.

00:13:27.072 --> 00:13:27.907
That's a lot of stuff.

00:13:28.073 --> 00:13:29.975
So, what's in the Boston
Kreme doughnut, you ask?

00:13:29.975 --> 00:13:31.877
All right, the dough is the
same as the glazed dough,

00:13:31.877 --> 00:13:35.247
but the Bavarian cream filling is

00:13:35.247 --> 00:13:37.550
water, sugar, modified food starch,

00:13:37.550 --> 00:13:38.751
corn syrup, palm oil,

00:13:38.751 --> 00:13:40.753
and it contains 2% or less of

00:13:41.921 --> 00:13:44.290
sucrose esters,

00:13:44.623 --> 00:13:46.859
natural and artificial flavors,

00:13:46.859 --> 00:13:48.327
oh, my God,

00:13:48.327 --> 00:13:49.361
glucono

00:13:49.361 --> 00:13:50.629
delta

00:13:50.629 --> 00:13:51.463
lact-

00:13:51.463 --> 00:13:54.400
I mean, they're just making
fun of me at this point.

00:13:54.400 --> 00:13:55.868
Glucono

00:13:55.868 --> 00:13:57.069
delta

00:13:57.069 --> 00:13:58.637
- lactone.

00:13:59.305 --> 00:14:00.873
Sounds like a font.

00:14:00.873 --> 00:14:02.708
Salt, potassium sorbate

00:14:02.708 --> 00:14:05.644
and sodium benzonate for preservatives,

00:14:05.644 --> 00:14:09.281
and agar, and beta-carotene for color.

00:14:09.582 --> 00:14:11.650
And, of course, don't forget
about the chocolate icing,

00:14:11.650 --> 00:14:13.118
which is sugar, water,

00:14:13.118 --> 00:14:15.154
cocoa, high-fructose corn syrup,

00:14:15.154 --> 00:14:16.822
soybean oil, cornstarch,

00:14:16.822 --> 00:14:18.424
corn syrup, maltodextrin,

00:14:18.424 --> 00:14:20.993
and contains 2% or less of dextrose,

00:14:20.993 --> 00:14:22.194
palm oil, salt,

00:14:22.194 --> 00:14:25.497
potassium sorbate and sodium propionate

00:14:25.497 --> 00:14:27.066
(preservatives), soy lecithin,

00:14:27.066 --> 00:14:29.435
artificial flavors, and agar.

00:14:29.435 --> 00:14:30.269
And you know what?

00:14:30.269 --> 00:14:31.704
I'm not going through every doughnut.

